			<div class="head">
								<div class="title" id="post-title-4832499">
																	<a href="/forum/t-13885797/seeking-greenlight-on-my-idea#post-4832499">Re: Seeking Greenlight On My Idea</a>
									</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/cybersqyd" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5336470); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=5336470&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606744381" alt="cybersqyd" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=5336470)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/cybersqyd" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5336470); return false;" >cybersqyd</a></span> <span class="odate time_1606742465 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">30 Nov 2020 13:21</span>
																	<br/>
						in discussion <a href="/forum/c-89000/help:ideas-critique">Writing Help / Help: Ideas Critique</a> &raquo;
						<a href="/forum/t-13885797/seeking-greenlight-on-my-idea">Seeking Greenlight On My Idea</a>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4832499">
									

<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">[+]&nbsp;Open&nbsp;for&nbsp;crit</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>I have a multitude of ideas for these interviews which (as I haven't begun writing them yet) aren't super fleshed out, but have, what I think is, a good basis.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>My concern with the ones you've listed out is that it feels like it's lacking a sense of coherence: they don't feel like they're building off each other so much as like, four completely separate interviews that could fit in any order.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>I understand the &quot;Native American curse&quot; concept may be somewhat overdone</p>
</blockquote>
<p>It is both <em>really</em> overdone and pretty problematic and I would urge you to not do this.</p>
<p>That said: the core story of the person here is the most interesting aspect of this to the point where I'd probably focus the story around like&#8230;what drove them to do this and how it gets wrapped and stuff; everything before this feels like a really lengthy preamble that doesn't add a tonne, y'know?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Everything after that in the log, will be mostly excluded/expunged, menial information (pH testing, and marking the times the fountains appear) as to avoid massive exposition.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I'd probably suggest not putting a tonne of menial information in this, or massive expunged sections: at the end of the day, you're wanting to write something interesting for a person to read and not a complete accounting on this.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>An addendum will tie things up, from one of the interviewers, warning that further disruption of the phenomenon could be genocidal</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This feels&#8230;overblown? Like, it's a relatively localised phenomenon and so it doesn't feel like this is a credible threat. But even if it did, having someone just kinda&#8230;say that this is the case feels like it'd be a really underwhelming way to show it?</p>
<hr />
<p>I think my strongest advice is to focus this arc on the person who made it; and why they made it, and how like, the Foundations attempts to contain this/the person affect it's working. Like the angle of the foundation bringing him into containment and then the fountain killing a bunch of folk is interesting, particularly if we can kinda see the maker go through an arc where e.g. they realise they made a mistake here or something?</p>
</div>
</div>
