			<div class="content" id="post-content-4832475">
									

<p>Deleted an article by <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/stolle-7b" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(7061608); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=7061608&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606741886" alt="Stolle 7B" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=7061608)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/stolle-7b" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(7061608); return false;">Stolle 7B</a></span> at -21 with three staff votes, standard deletion process.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Description: SCP-5392 is a humanoid creature resembling a young female adult approximately 3.06 meters tall with long arms stretching its entire body length and legs 0.96 meters tall. Despite being humanoid SCP-5392 shows no signs of human intelligence or speech, only mumbling unrecognizable language in raspy utterance. SCP-5392 has long, silky, black hair and its epidermis is completely gray in color. It wears a pale, torn, ragged dress, appearing to be a wedding dress. Its face is long and thin, with pale beady eyes and no nose. Its mouth is full of thin, jagged teeth, but has no tongue. The inside of SCP-5392 is completely epidermis, with no muscle, bone, or organs. Origins of this creature are still unknown.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>No feedback present.</p>
<hr />
<p>Deleted an article by <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/agent-dragnel" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6581177); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=6581177&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606741886" alt="Agent Dragnel" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=6581177)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/agent-dragnel" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6581177); return false;">Agent Dragnel</a></span> at -19 with three staff votes, standard deletion process.</p>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>Description:</strong> SCP 5655 is an elderly male measuring 2.12 metres in height, SCP 5655 wears a red drizabone which has multiple toys and bells dating from the 1950’s attached to the exterior. All toys show signs of corrosion and rot. SCP 5655 has high levels of pigmentation and obesity. The hands of SCP 5655 are normally worn by mildly damaged Christmas mittens, SCP 5655 will only take these mittens off when aggressive. SCP 5655 hands suffer from severe frostbite and overgrown nails ranging 2-4 centimetres in length, it is unclear how the fingers of SCP-5655 remain attatched.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Feedback is as follows:</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Karakatt</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;Karakatt</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Howdy hey</p>
<p>As stated before posting:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Remember: The main site is for summary judgment of final work, not feedback and critique on unfinished work.</p>
<p>It is your responsibility to post only finished, final work. Site members are not required to justify or explain their votes.</p>
<p>If you understand all of the above and still wish to create this page, click here to do so.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Readers are not required to review your articles since the site is for finished works only. It was your responsibility to receive critique by our <a href="http://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/chat-guide">IRC Chats</a> or our <a href="http://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/forum/c-89000/help:ideas-critique">idea critique forums</a>.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Greenburger</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;Greenburger</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>This one has a lot of issues, but lets start with the positive. I like the idea of a decomposed justice-loving Santa. But your execution leaves a lot to be desired.</p>
<p>Firstly, there are a couple of plot holes. There are probably millions of crimes committed in the month of December in just America alone. If this SCP showed up for every single one, the foundation would have a serious problem preventing the public from finding out about it. To fix this, perhaps you can change the article so that this scp only appears for extremely heinous crimes.</p>
<p>The same goes for instances where the scp shows up to give people presents. The scp showing up to give people presents could result in the public finding out about anomalies. The foundation needs a way to prevent the public from finding out, so either remove this bit or add a way for the scp foundation to track the scp so they can amnesticize individuals who were exposed.</p>
<p>The concepts also leaves a lot of unanswered questions. For instance, can the scp be in two places at once? If a bunch of people commit a crime at the same time but in different places, will the scp appear for only one person, or will a manifestation of the scp appear for all of the people.</p>
<p>Another question is if people have to &quot;fix their unlawful act&quot; for the scp to leave them alone, what counts as fixing an unlawful act. If you murdered someone, would you need to find a way to bring the person you murdered back to life. You need to create a specific set of rules that can be applied universally.</p>
<p>Additionally, you never specify what powers the scp has. Can it teleport? What if you try to fight it while the scp is trying to disembowel you. Does it have a way to immobilize its targets through combat or an afflicted paralysis? That needs to be specified.</p>
<p>Finally, why do people exposed to the scp need to be killed if any unlawful act can summon the scp? That seems excessive and inefficient, which is why the foundation wouldn't do it. It seems more likely that the foundation would investigate what those individuals did and determine and appropriate response. Additionally, why does the tree as well as the dishes/containers for the milk and cookies need to be incinerated. You said that was to prevent contamination, but I thought the scp only affected individuals who did unlawful acts. Is the scp diseased or something?</p>
<p>Overall, there are lots of unanswered questions and glaring plot holes.</p>
<p>There are also lots of issues with you grammar scattered throughout the article. I'm not going to list them all since this is already a long post, but one example is in the very first sentence, where you use &quot;is&quot; when you should use &quot;are&quot;. There are several other mistakes like this throughout the article</p>
<p>You also have a bad habit of making your sentences to long by writing in a very indirect and convoluted way. For instance, you wrote:</p>
<p>&quot;SCP 5655 will manifest nearby an individual who has committed an unlawful act in the duration of the month December.&quot;</p>
<p>The first issue is that you tend to use a conjugation of &quot;is&quot; before every verb in this sentence (manifest and commit). You should do that sparingly at most. It would be better like this:</p>
<p>&quot;SCP 5655 manifests near individuals who commit unlawful acts in the duration of the month December.&quot;</p>
<p>Another way to cut down on fluff is at the very end of that sentence, where you wrote &quot;in the duration of the month of December&quot;. &quot;In the duration of&quot; is just a long and convoluted way of saying during, so that can be shortened to &quot;during the month of December&quot;, giving us the final edited version of that sentence:</p>
<p>&quot;SCP 5655 manifests near individuals who commit unlawful acts during the month December.&quot;</p>
<p>Writing it like this is clearer and more concise. Most of your sentences have issues like this, which makes the overall article sound unprofessional. That takes away from the immersion of the entry, since the foundation is supposed to be all about cold professionalism.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<hr />
<p>Deleted an article by <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/bruh-my-yeezys" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2996049); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2996049&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606741886" alt="bruh my yeezys" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2996049)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/bruh-my-yeezys" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2996049); return false;">bruh my yeezys</a></span> at -17 with three staff votes, standard deletion process.</p>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>Description:</strong> SCP-5645 is a humanoid superficially resembling an afro-latino male in late adulthood. It is outfitted with a ████ brand beige fedora and suit adorned with a laurel green tie. Although SCP-5645 possesses wireframe glasses, it is unknown if it suffers from Hyperopia. Its primary language is spanish.</p>
</blockquote>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Elunerazim</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;Elunerazim</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>While posting multiple times is major no-no, I honestly think this is a not-bad SCP and I think there's a lot of potential. Fixed a typo for ya, too ;).</p>
<p>+1, but the multitude of posts will likely get it deleted.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Scorpion451</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;Scorpion451</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>There are a number of problems here, but the primary one is that this is <em>merely</em> a description.</p>
<p>SCPs are speculative fiction stories presented in the form of archival documents. Some are vignettes that paint an evocative scene over the course of a few paragraphs, some are sweeping multiple act novellas with twisting plots, some tell their stories through the ways that they toy with the framing itself&#8230; but at its core, every SCP is a story. <em>That</em> is the point of an SCP.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Quicksilvers</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;Quicksilvers</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Very interesting idea, but there are a few logical plot holes.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>These noises include memetic kill-words such as “Cekliption”, “Diffechindic”, “Humplionicaned”, etcetera.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Why would you specifically spell out memetic kill agents in a document? Even if its a LVL5 one like you stated, that could count as something very volatile and dangerous.</p>
<p>I feel like you could really expand upon this concept - why does this SCP display the Berryman-Langford agent specifically if the agent is so volatile and used for one of the Foundation's most buried secrets? Why is it spreading it around? Is it trying to inoculate people against SCP-001's safety protocols? Is it trying to use them to kill people? I really hope that this gets a rewrite because I love the concept and it has so much potential.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Mikaelious</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;Mikaelious</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>An SCP-5645 escape is designated an AK-Class Omega-Cognitohazard Scenario. It is in the best interests for the foundation and humanity that this does not happen.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I feel like the latter sentence could be cut off or altered; surely the Foundation employees know that an apocalyptic event is something they should try to prevent.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<hr />
<p>Deleted an article by <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/misaka321" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(7056350); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=7056350&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606741886" alt="Misaka321" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=7056350)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/misaka321" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(7056350); return false;">Misaka321</a></span> at -12 with three staff votes, standard deletion process.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Cypher is a new agent.</p>
<p>It is what it is, spirited young man takes over the mantle of his father, a Foundation agent who died long ago. Educated at home, Cypher joined the foundation — and after watching a Foundation promotional video, he felt a sense of meaning in his life. So like a dozen other newcomers, he trains, tests — and hopes one day to &quot;save the world,&quot; as the promo puts it.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Feedback is as follows:</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Asdfaslas</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;Asdfaslas</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>There's definitely a lot to unpack here but for some reason the thing that I feel like it's most important to tell you? &quot;Eight pairs of eyes&quot; is actually 8 people. Not 4 people. I can't explain why that bothered me the most, but it did.</p>
<p>I'm not sure why you used weird open circles instead of periods a couple times, out of nowhere. I hope you look through the style guides because many many things should've been capitalized that weren't (Foundation, Chaos Insurgency, probably other stuff I've lost track of already) and most of all I hope someone a bit more useful can come by and give you more detailed advice than I just did, because I can tell that you really cared and really tried here and I'm just not cut out to really help much.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Vivarium</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;Vivarium</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>I personally think the biggest problem with this article is the fact that you are telling a lot more then you're showing. I feel like there is a lot of potential in this concept, so I highly recomend you take this idea to the <a href="http://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/forum/c-89000">Idea Critique Forum</a>, and seek Critique from other more experienced authors then myself. I hope you give this another shot.</p>
</div>
</div>
