						in discussion <a href="/forum/c-50742/per-page-discussions">Per Page Discussions / Per page discussions</a> &raquo;
						<a href="/scp-576/comments/show">SCP-576</a>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4832453">
									

<p>This was fine. Competently executed, and an alright idea. However, the strings of my heart were distinctly un-tugged.</p>
<p>Part of it, I think, was the repetition between the interview logs (recalled in an intensely weird way for people who are prisoners being used as human guinea pigs) and the final documentation, neither providing, so far as I could glean, any additional information. There's also the, in my opinion, rather pointless addendum, which adds nothing to the story.</p>
<p>My main issue, though, is that struck me less as a wistful reminder of half-forgotten memories, and more as forced sentimentality. Maybe I've spent too long reading the comment sections for YouTube mixes with names like &quot;I ' M S O A L O N E&quot; and &quot;N O S T A L G I C A T 2&#160;A M&quot;<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-465955-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-465955-1')">1</a></sup> but my reaction to the memories was less &quot;I will never get these moments back&quot; and more &quot;Oh, I have read this exact comment thirty times before.&quot;</p>
<p>I'm glad that this has been enjoyable for a lot of people, but I am not a fan. -1</p>
<div class="footnotes-footer">
<div class="title">Footnotes</div>
<div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-465955-1"><a href="javascript:;" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnoteref-465955-1')">1</a>. Also, yes, this obviously pre-dates that whole genre of videos by several years, but I'm just trying to provide context my reaction.</div>
</div>

